@startuml Linkwise_Modem_Recovery
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam Padding 8
skinparam defaultFontName "Latin Modern Roman"
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam ArrowColor #2A9D8F
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 25
top to bottom direction
state "Active sender" as Active {
 state "Ready\nqueued bytes owned" as Ready
 state "Sending DATA\nlocal token / TX watchdog" as Sending
 state "Await validated answer\nreceive-window binding" as Waiting
 state "Sending state query\nDATA not repeated" as Query
 state "Retired once\nnext queued block" as Acked
 [*] --> Ready
 Ready -right-> Sending : start
 Sending -right-> Waiting : TX complete
 Waiting --> Acked : Delivered
 Acked --> Ready : next block
 Waiting --> Sending : NotDelivered\nretry budget remains
 Waiting --> Query : answer deadline\nquery budget remains
 Query --> Waiting : query TX complete
}
state "Faulted\nunresolved bytes retained" as Fault
state "Aborted\nqueue discarded" as Abort
Active --> Fault : TX failure / watchdog\nquery or retry budget exhausted
Active --> Abort : explicit abort
Fault --> Abort : explicit abort
note bottom of Active
 Implemented event-level sender; runtime integration remains proposed.
 Qualified TX complete requires presentation and release/turnaround.
 Client channel loss cancels; restart/reconnect never replays bytes.
 Unresolved retention is in memory, not crash durability.
 Local tokens are not on-air sequence numbers.
end note
@enduml
